<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">1988 Armenian earthquake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Spitak earthquake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1988 Armenian earthquake struck northern Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> on 7 December 1988 with a magnitude of about 6.8, destroying the town of Spitak and heavily damaging Leninakan, now Gyumri. At least 25,000 people were killed and hundreds of thousands left homeless. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> cut short a visit to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> accepted large-scale foreign aid.</p></div>
